doc.description:
Use navigation primitives to follow Extended Dubins path, that is Dubins paths which may start or end with an extra segment.

      If Mission mode is used, this module registers a mission called "DUBIN" using all 12 parameters as follows:
      ```
        ref_problem.start_p.x     = params[0];
        ref_problem.start_p.y     = params[1];
        ref_problem.start_p.theta = params[2];

        ref_problem.end_p.x       = params[3];
        ref_problem.end_p.y       = params[4];
        ref_problem.end_p.theta   = params[5];

        ref_problem.target_alt    = params[6];

        ref_problem.start_time    = params[7]; (time is in seconds, from GPS ToW)
        ref_problem.end_time      = params[8];

        ref_problem.type          = (int)params[9];
        ref_problem.radius        = params[10];
        ref_problem.extra         = params[11];
      ```
      This recomputes the full Dubins path from the given elements then follows it.

      It also registers a mission called "DUBEL" (for "Dubins Element") using the following parameters:
      ```
        solo_element.init_point.x = params[0];
        solo_element.init_point.y = params[1];
        solo_element.init_point.theta = params[2];
        solo_element.radius = params[3];
        solo_element.length = params[4];
        altitude = params[5];
      ```
      Only the given element is tracked, without any path recomputation.
